    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating an owner's `customerCode` on collision by appending `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nI implemented this with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **New cohesive unit** \u2014 `DeduplicateCustomerCode.java`, a single small function class (`WMC_other = 0`, low CC) that reads existing codes via `OwnerRepository.findAll()` and appends `-<n>` until unique. It follows the existing OfficeFloor idiom (`@Val Owner`, repository injection, `Out`/`@Val` state flow) used by neighbors like `CountNamesakes` and `RequireUniqueIdentity`.\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml` now routes `AssignCustomerCode \u2192 DeduplicateCustomerCode \u2192 CountNamesakes`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nI deliberately did **not** grow `AssignCustomerCode` (which would have paid the WMC of its `hash8` helper) \u2014 instead the new behavior lives in its own class with no surrounding complexity to hold. Only two files touched (one new class, one YAML wiring change), no existing function bodies modified.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
